Aim:
To write a Python program to perform basic tuple operations and to convert a tuple into a list and back into a tuple.

Algorithm:
Start
Create a tuple t containing the values 10, 20, 30, 40, 50.
Display the complete tuple.
Display the first element using index 0.
Display the last element using index -1.
Find and display the length of the tuple using len().
Count how many times 20 occurs using count().
Find the index position of 30 using index().
Find and display the maximum value using max().
Find and display the minimum value using min().
Find and display the sum of all elements using sum().
Check whether 40 is present in the tuple using the in operator.
Convert the tuple into a list using list().
Display the converted list.
Convert the list back into a tuple using tuple().
Display the converted tuple.
Stop.

Code:
t=(10,20,30,40,50)

print("tuple : ",t)
print("first element : ",t[0])
print("last element : ",t[-1])
print("length : ",len(t))
print("count of 20 : ",t.count(20))
print("index of 30 : ",t.index(30))
print("maximum : ",max(t))
print("minimum : ",min(t))
print("sum : ",sum(t))
print("is 40 present? ",40 in t)

#convert to list
l=list(t)
print("converted tuple to list",l)

#convert list back to tuple
t2=tuple(l)
print("list converted to tuple: ",t2)

